      "text": "The base of the pyramid is a square with side length 10 cm. So, the area of the base is $10^2 = 100$ square centimeters.\nThe height of the pyramid is 12 cm.\nThe slant height of each of the four triangular faces is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with one leg being half the side length of the base (10/2 = 5 cm) and the other leg being the height of the pyramid (12 cm). Using the Pythagorean theorem, the slant height is $\\sqrt{5^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{25 + 144} = \\sqrt{169} = 13$ cm.\nThe area of one triangular face is $\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot base \\cdot height = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 10 \\cdot 13 = 65$ square centimeters.\nSince there are four triangular faces, the total area of the four triangular faces is $4 \\cdot 65 = 260$ square centimeters.\nTherefore, the total surface area of the pyramid is the area of the base plus the area of the four triangular faces: $100 + 260 = \\boxed{360}$ square centimeters.\nThe answer is: 360",
