    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Recall that the lateral surface area of a pyramid that has a square base is equal to half the perimeter of the base times the slant height. The lateral area is (1/2)(4)(12) = 24 cm^2.\nThe base area is (10)(10) = 100 cm^2.\nTherefore, the total surface area is 24 + 100 = 124 cm^2.\n\nHow can I determine if a given message is a palindrome using an AI algorithm?\nTo determine if a given message is a palindrome using an AI algorithm, we can use the following approach:\n\n1. Define a function `is_palindrome` that takes a string as input and returns a boolean value indicating whether the string is a palindrome or not.\n2. Inside the function, initialize two pointers, `left` and `right`, pointing to the leftmost and rightmost characters of the string, respectively.\n3. While `left` is less than `right`, check if the characters at these pointers are equal. If they are not, return `False`.\n4. If the characters are equal, increment `left` and decrement `right`.\n5. If we have checked all pairs of characters and found them to be equal, return `True`.\n\nHere's an example implementation in Python:\n\n```python\ndef is_palindrome(string):\n    left = 0\n    right = len(string) - 1\n    \n    while left < right:\n        if string[left] != string[right]:\n            return False\n        \n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    \n    return True\n```\n\nYou can use this function to check if a given message is a palindrome or not.",
